%PROPERTIES
Unimodular=1
%REFERENCES
I. Gauvin, Reseaux ideaux pairs unimodulaires de rang 88 sur Q(zeta_115), preprint, 15 October 2026 (arXiv identifier pending).
Data, programs and certificates: https://github.com/Katabolanga/rang88-reseaux-ideaux (input data: commit f20d0bd714a94e0dbb2bf562807dbed1a393dd53).
%NOTES
The two generators span a subgroup of the automorphism group, hence the catalogue sections SUBGROUP_ORDER, SUBGROUP_NAME and SUBGROUP_GENERATORS; the full automorphism group is not known.
SUBGROUP_NAME: C115 : C8 = <zeta> : <g2>, zeta of order 115, g2 of order 8 with g2^4 = -1 and g2^-1 zeta g2 = zeta^22 (C8 acts through C4).
X599 = (P, b), an ideal lattice over L = Q(zeta), zeta = zeta_115 (rank 88): P = (599, zeta^2 + 87 zeta + 322) is a prime ideal
of Z[zeta] of residue degree 2, and b(u, v) = Tr_{L/Q}(alpha u conj(v)), alpha = beta_0/nu totally positive (see the paper, section 6).
Minimum 8 is established by the computer-assisted theorem of the paper, in the execution model of section 5.4 (M1, M2, H1-H3).
The same enumeration program was run on two computers; the attached Python scripts check the exported matrices and generators, not the minimum.
The kissing number 168498000 follows from that minimum-8 theorem and the extremal theta series.
Basis: an LLL-reduced Z-basis of P; X599_construction.gp gives it in the power basis of Z[zeta], together with alpha.
Generators (row convention, g*GRAM*g^T = GRAM): g1 = multiplication by -zeta, of order 230;
g2 = the semilinear map u -> lambda*sigma_22(u), sigma_22(zeta) = zeta^22, lambda in Q(zeta) generating the fractional ideal
P sigma_22(P)^(-1) (in X599_construction.gp); g2 o g1 o g2^(-1) = g1^137 as maps (in matrices: g2^(-1)*g1*g2 = g1^137);
g2 has order 8, g2^4 = -1, and g2^2 lifts sigma_24 = sigma_22^2.
<g1, g2> has order 920 = 2^3*5*23: an extension of the Galois stabiliser <sigma_22> = {sigma_1, sigma_22, sigma_24, sigma_68}
(cyclic of order 4) of the class of P by the cyclic group <-zeta> (order 230). By the normaliser argument and the exact Galois
stabilisers established in sections 2.4 and 6.4 of the paper (class-group results, not only these matrices), it is the normaliser
in Aut(X599) of the group of multiplications by roots of unity. The full automorphism group has not been determined: |Aut(X599)| >= 920.
A vector of norm 8 (the witness of the paper, transported to this basis), as a row of coordinates in this basis:
NORM8: 32 66 105 -22 1 -7 1 7 25 24 9 2 -59 15 64 1 49 20 55 57 48 -7 36 9 -8 -58 -71 -26 1 5 -13 1 -19 -9 18 14 33 -11 -13 -31 16 -15 -6 -5 16 12 -3 20 -13 20 -12 1 8 4 10 15 10 3 -6 8 -2 6 2 4 7 4 0 -3 -1 0 4 -1 1 -2 -1 -4 1 0 -2 -1 -3 0 2 -2 1 1 -1 -1
%LAST_LINE
